mac_ax: use div_u64() for 64-bit division so the module links on ARM32

Fixes a hard build failure on this board (ARMv7 Cortex-A9). Upstream's
c2h_wicense_rpt_info() divides a 64-bit value by a constant with the plain C
`/` operator:

    en_dis_time_ms = (u32)((((u64)rpt->en_dis_time_h << 32) + rpt->en_dis_time_l) / 1000);

On any 32-bit architecture gcc cannot lower a 64-bit division inline, so it
emits a call to a libgcc/EABI helper -- `__aeabi_uldivmod` on ARM. The kernel
does not export that symbol to modules, so the build dies at modpost, AFTER
every object has compiled cleanly:

    ERROR: modpost: "__aeabi_uldivmod" [8852cu.ko] undefined!

That is why upstream ships it: the driver's own README tests against x86_64
and aarch64, where `/` on a u64 compiles to a native instruction and the bug is
invisible. It is not a Realtek-vs-us disagreement, just an untested target.

`div_u64()` (linux/math64.h) is the kernel's portable spelling for exactly this
-- u64 numerator, u32 denominator -- and compiles to the same native divide on
64-bit while routing through __do_div64 on 32-bit. Semantics are identical; the
values here are a microsecond counter scaled to milliseconds, well inside u32
after division.

Not using the driver's own _os_division64() (phl/pltfm_ops_linux.h), which
would otherwise be the in-idiom choice: it lives in the phl/ platform-ops layer
and is not reachable from phl/hal_g6/mac/mac_ax/, whose PLTFM_* macro set
(phl/hal_g6/mac/mac_def.h) offers no division helper at all. A direct
linux/math64.h include is the smaller change and needs no new layering.

Affects a debug/telemetry printer ("[WisenseRpt] ...") only, so there is no
behavioural risk beyond the two values it prints.

Upstream status: not submitted. morrownr/rtl8852cu-20251113 is a vendor-drop
mirror that takes no patches; carry locally. Re-check on every version bump --
if upstream ever fixes it, this patch will fail to apply and say so loudly,
which is the outcome we want.

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>

--- a/phl/hal_g6/mac/mac_ax/fwcmd.c
+++ b/phl/hal_g6/mac/mac_ax/fwcmd.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
  *
  ******************************************************************************/
 
+#include <linux/math64.h>
 #include "fwcmd.h"
 #include "mcc.h"
 #include "mac_priv.h"
@@ -2144,8 +2145,8 @@
 
 	PLTFM_MEMCPY(rpt, pkg, sizeof(struct rtw_hal_mac_wicense_rpt));
 
-	en_dis_time_ms = (u32)((((u64)rpt->en_dis_time_h << 32) + rpt->en_dis_time_l) / 1000);
-	active_time_ms = (u32)((((u64)rpt->active_time_h << 32) + rpt->active_time_l) / 1000);
+	en_dis_time_ms = (u32)div_u64((((u64)rpt->en_dis_time_h << 32) + rpt->en_dis_time_l), 1000);
+	active_time_ms = (u32)div_u64((((u64)rpt->active_time_h << 32) + rpt->active_time_l), 1000);
 
 	if (csi_info->dbg_rpt_mode == WICENSE_DBG_RPT_MODE_EN_DETAIL) {
 		PLTFM_MSG_ALWAYS("[WisenseRpt] ===> report start....\n");
